        "parms": "# controlchange and xctlout — knobs to a MIDI port\ncontrolchange builds a control-change message for midiout: each value 0-127 on its inlet sends one. Its arguments are the channel, counted from 0, and the controller number: controlchange 0 1 is the modulation wheel on channel 1. xctlout sends a value of 0-16383 as two messages, the coarse half on a controller 0-31 and the fine half on that number plus 32. midiout's argument is the output port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. You hear something only when a synthesizer listens on that port.\nMax's ctlout takes the controller first and the channel, 1-16, second, and sends to a port itself. Here the channel comes first, counted from 0, and midiout sends.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
