        "parms": "5. xmidiin 0 shows each message that arrives on input port 0 as numbers, one list per message, and print writes every one to the log (Ctrl+J). 176 1 64 is controller 1 at 64 on channel 1. xctlout sends two messages per value, so the box shows the fine one, on controller 33. On Linux, output 0 and input 0 are usually Midi Through, which sends back whatever it receives, so you see what you send. Elsewhere, set both arguments to a loopback port.",
